  {
    "ref": "3.5 SolvedEx.4",
    "bucket": "solved",
    "format": "subjective",
    "subtopic": "Remainder Theorem",
    "difficulty": "MODERATE",
    "stem": "If the polynomial \\(t^3 - 3t^2 + kt + 50\\) is divided by \\((t - 3)\\), the remainder is 62. Find the value of \\(k\\).",
    "solution": "When given polynomial is divided by \\((t - 3)\\) the remainder is 62. It means the value of the polynomial when \\(t = 3\\) is 62.\n\\(p(t) = t^3 - 3t^2 + kt + 50\\)\nBy remainder theorem,\nRemainder \\(= p(3) = 3^3 - 3 \\times 3^2 + k \\times 3 + 50\\)\n\\(= 27 - 3 \\times 9 + 3k + 50\\)\n\\(= 27 - 27 + 3k + 50\\)\n\\(= 3k + 50\\)\nBut remainder is 62.\n\\(\\therefore 3k + 50 = 62\\)\n\\(\\therefore 3k = 62 - 50\\)\n\\(\\therefore 3k = 12\\)\n\\(\\therefore k = \\dfrac{12}{3}\\)\n\\(\\therefore k = 4\\)"
  },
  {
    "ref": "3.5 SolvedEx.5",
    "bucket": "solved",
    "format": "subjective",
    "subtopic": "Factor Theorem",
    "difficulty": "EASY",
    "stem": "If \\(p(x) = (x^3 + 4x - 5)\\) is divided by \\((x - 1)\\) then find the remainder and hence determine whether \\((x - 1)\\) is a factor of \\(p(x)\\) or not ?",
    "solution": "\\(p(x) = x^3 + 4x - 5\\)\n\\(p(1) = (1)^3 + 4(1) - 5\\)\n\\(= 1 + 4 - 5\\)\n\\(= 0\\)\nAs per the remainder theorem, Remainder \\(= 0\\)\n\\(\\therefore (x - 1)\\) is a factor of \\(p(x)\\)."
  },
  {
    "ref": "3.5 SolvedEx.6",
    "bucket": "solved",
    "format": "subjective",
    "subtopic": "Factor Theorem",
    "difficulty": "EASY",
    "stem": "If \\(p(x) = x^3 + 4x - 5\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\) then find the remainder and hence determine whether \\((x + 2)\\) is a factor of \\(p(x)\\) or not.",
    "solution": "\\(p(x) = x^3 + 4x - 5\\)\n\\(p(-2) = (-2)^3 + 4(-2) - 5\\)\n\\(p(-2) = -8 - 8 - 5\\)\n\\(= -21\\)\nAs per the remainder theorem, Remainder \\(= -21\\) \\(\\therefore\\) Remainder \\(\\neq 0\\)\n\\(\\therefore (x + 2)\\) is not a factor of \\(p(x)\\)."
  },
  {
    "ref": "3.5 SolvedEx.7",
    "bucket": "solved",
    "format": "subjective",
    "subtopic": "Factor Theorem",
    "difficulty": "EASY",
    "stem": "Check whether \\(x - 2\\) is a factor of the polynomial \\(x^3 - x^2 - 4\\) by using factor theorem.",
    "solution": "\\(p(x) = x^3 - x^2 - 4\\)  Divisor \\(= x - 2\\)\n\\(\\therefore p(2) = 2^3 - 2^2 - 4 = 8 - 4 - 4 = 0\\)\n\\(\\therefore\\) By factor theorem \\((x - 2)\\) is a factor of the polynomial \\((x^3 - x^2 - 4)\\)."
  },
  {
    "ref": "3.5 SolvedEx.8",
    "bucket": "solved",
    "format": "subjective",
    "subtopic": "Factor Theorem",
    "difficulty": "MODERATE",
    "stem": "If \\((x - 1)\\) is the factor of the polynomial \\((x^3 - 2x^2 + mx - 4)\\) then find the value of \\(m\\).",
    "solution": "\\((x - 1)\\) is factor of \\(p(x)\\). \\(\\therefore p(1) = 0\\)\n\\(p(x) = x^3 - 2x^2 + mx - 4\\)\n\\(p(1) = 1^3 - 2 \\times 1^2 + m \\times 1 - 4 = 0\\)\n\\(\\therefore 1 - 2 \\times 1 + m - 4 = 0\\)\n\\(\\therefore 1 - 2 + m - 4 = 0\\)  \\(\\therefore m - 5 = 0\\)  \\(\\therefore m = 5\\)"
  },

